WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.537
This example uses an alias with Python's

00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:06.211
statistics module The first line says import

00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:09.382
statistics as stats This means that for

00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:11.118
the rest of the program we can

00:00:11.132 --> 00:00:13.303
refer to the statistics module using the

00:00:13.316 --> 00:00:16.592
shorter name stats Next we create a

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:19.842
list called scores The list contains five

00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:24.197
values eighty-two ninety seventy-six eighty-eight
and ninety-five

00:00:25.132 --> 00:00:29.303
Then we calculate several summary statistics Stats

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.237
dot mean calculates the arithmetic average Stats

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.855
dot median calculates the middle value after

00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:38.671
the scores are ordered We also use

00:00:38.697 --> 00:00:41.053
the built-in minimum and maximum functions to

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.171
find the smallest and largest values The

00:00:44.197 --> 00:00:46.750
range is calculated by subtracting the lowest

00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:49.750
score from the highest score Before you

00:00:49.776 --> 00:00:51.645
run the code try to predict some

00:00:51.671 --> 00:00:54.395
of the output The highest score is

00:00:54.408 --> 00:00:59.737
ninety-five The lowest score is seventy-six
Therefore

00:00:59.921 --> 00:01:02.934
the range should be nineteen Now click

00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:05.566
the Run button You should see the

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:08.895
original list of scores The average should

00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:12.158
be eighty-six point two The median should

00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:15.697
be eighty-eight The range should be nineteen

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.553
This is a small example but it

00:01:18.566 --> 00:01:22.197
represents a common analytics pattern We start

00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:24.289
with a collection of values then use

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:28.013
reusable functions to summarize the data Now

00:01:28.026 --> 00:01:31.105
try a small change Add another score

00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:33.039
to the list such as one hundred

00:01:33.974 --> 00:01:35.645
Run the cell again and observe how

00:01:35.671 --> 00:01:39.171
the average median and range change The

00:01:39.184 --> 00:01:41.526
main lesson is not the specific numbers

00:01:42.461 --> 00:01:44.026
The lesson is that an alias can

00:01:44.053 --> 00:01:45.921
make repeated use of a module more

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.776
readable while still making it clear where

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:48.882
the functions come from
